== Problem 4 (uncapped, start (0,1)) ==
ok   from (0,1) the only bucket you can take from is bucket 2
ok   refill 9 on the first move gives a game of exactly 10 moves (forced after move 1)
ok   refill 29 on the first move gives a game of exactly 30 moves (forced after move 1)
ok   refill 99 on the first move gives a game of exactly 100 moves (forced after move 1)
ok   refill 999 on the first move gives a game of exactly 1000 moves (forced after move 1)
  So the possible lengths from (0,1) are exactly 1, 2, 3, ... (refill M gives M+1): every finite number is beaten,
  every play is finite, and no single bound covers all plays.

